# Mutations for the Kotlin lowered-artifact lane.
#
# What these guard is the sentence `ecma262-lowered-kotlin` says about itself:
# that a Kotlin artifact generated with `--script-engine lua` was COMPILED and
# RUN, and answered the shared ECMA-262 table.
#
# ⚠ The runner cannot drive Gradle, so what is judged here is the RUST half —
# the registry row that makes the gate reachable, the supersession
# classification that keeps the workflow honest, and the gate script's own
# structural claims held by `gate_registry_contract`. The JVM half of the lane
# is bought by hand, the way `kotlin_engine_selection.cases` says the Kotlin
# side always has to be: this backend has no gradle runner in `scripts/mutate`.
#
# ⚠ Target selectors, never a bare filter: a filter reaches every binary the
# selector matched.
mutation_tests -p sce-build --features cli \
    --test gate_registry_contract --test ci_supersession_policy
mutation_runtime_targets scripts/gates/ecma262-lowered-kotlin.sh \
    .github/workflows/ecma262-lowered-kotlin.yml \
    tools/git-hooks/gate_registry.py
# ⚠ COMPILED, so `mutation_targets` and not the runtime list. One case removes
# this lane's row from the `LANES` table, and that table lives inside the
# oracle's own source file. Measured 2026-08-30: declared in neither list, the
# case came back INCONCLUSIVE with `the case body did not apply` — only
# declared files are snapshotted, so the runner refuses to edit one it could
# not restore. A case that cannot apply is not a case that survived, and the
# two read differently only because the runner says so.
mutation_targets sce-build/tests/ci_supersession_policy.rs

# ── The lane stops being reachable ─────────────────────────────────
#
# A gate nothing selects is a gate that never runs, and the failure is silent:
# `scripts/gate` would refuse the slug, the pre-push hook would never choose
# it, and CI's own job would be the only thing left measuring the artifact.
# `gate_registry_contract` holds every gate to having a workflow that runs it.

mutation_case "the lowered Kotlin gate loses the workflow that runs it" <<'PY'
edit("tools/git-hooks/gate_registry.py",
     '"ecma262-lowered-kotlin": {\n        "workflows": ["ecma262-lowered-kotlin.yml"],',
     '"ecma262-lowered-kotlin": {\n        "workflows": [],')
PY

# ── A new lane slips past the supersession policy ──────────────────
#
# `ci_supersession_policy` classifies EVERY workflow in the directory and reds
# one nobody classified. That is the check a NEW lane is most likely to walk
# past, because adding a file is not adding a row — and an unclassified lane
# neither supersedes nor queues by anyone's decision.

mutation_case "the new lane is added without being classified" <<'PY'
edit("sce-build/tests/ci_supersession_policy.rs",
     '    ("ecma262-lowered-kotlin.yml", 4.8, 0, 0),',
     '')
PY

# ── The gate stops proving the two artifacts are different ─────────
#
# THE case that matters. Both artifacts answer the same 98 cases and — with
# both divergence arrays empty — answer them identically, so the suite alone
# cannot tell a real pair from a subject compared against itself. The floor on
# the subject's lowered call sites is the only thing that can: a
# `--script-engine lua` that accepted the flag and emitted the default anyway
# produces two identical machines whose counts both sit down at the run-time
# helper's single arm, and every case in them still passes.
#
# Dropping the floor to zero leaves the mirror equalities intact — identical
# machines mirror each other perfectly — which is exactly why the floor is a
# separate claim and not a corollary of them.

mutation_case "the lowered artifact may carry no lowered call site at all" <<'PY'
edit("scripts/gates/ecma262-lowered-kotlin.sh",
     "if (( lowered_lua < 50 )); then",
     "if (( lowered_lua < 0 )); then")
PY

# ── The census stops being required ────────────────────────────────
#
# The lane's verdict is read from the run's OUTPUT, and Gradle answers an
# unchanged `test` task UP-TO-DATE without producing any. Measured 2026-08-30:
# the second invocation of this gate reported no census over a perfectly good
# artifact, because nothing had run. `--rerun` is what makes the run happen and
# the census demand is what notices when it does not.

mutation_case "a run that produced no census is accepted" <<'PY'
edit("scripts/gates/ecma262-lowered-kotlin.sh",
     '[ -n "$census" ] \\',
     '[ -n "$census" ] || true \\')
PY

mutation_case "the suite is allowed to answer from cache instead of running" <<'PY'
edit("scripts/gates/ecma262-lowered-kotlin.sh",
     "./gradlew --console=plain :sce-kotlin-lowered-ecma262:test --rerun \\",
     "./gradlew --console=plain :sce-kotlin-lowered-ecma262:test \\")
PY

# ── The workflow stops naming the pin the gate reads ───────────────
#
# `sce_gate_require_jdk` derives its floor from this workflow's
# `java-version:`. A workflow that stopped declaring one would leave the gate
# with no floor and Gradle free to run on whatever JVM the machine exports —
# which on this fleet has been a JDK 8 while `java --version` said 17.

mutation_case "the workflow stops pinning the JDK the gate derives its floor from" <<'PY'
edit(".github/workflows/ecma262-lowered-kotlin.yml",
     "        java-version: '17'",
     "        java-version: ''")
PY

# ── The exclusion list loses its ceiling ───────────────────────────
#
# `kotlin_lowered_artifact_defects.json` is the one thing in this lane that can
# make it green while the artifact answers ECMA-262 wrong, so the ceiling on it
# is held from two sources. The suite's `MAX_DEFECTS` lives in the same file as
# the assertion that reads it — raise the constant and the assertion agrees
# with you — so the gate keeps its own, in another language, over the count the
# suite PRINTED. Removing it leaves the list free to grow to the size of the
# population, at which point every case is excused and the lane is green over
# an artifact that answers nothing.

mutation_case "the exclusion list may grow without limit" <<'PY'
edit("scripts/gates/ecma262-lowered-kotlin.sh",
     "if (( excused > DEFECT_CEILING )); then",
     "if (( excused > 10000 )); then")
PY
